{"base_rate":0.2469879518072289,"brier":0.13717786144578314,"bss":0.26242475121951214,"bss_hi":0.36079565745823255,"bss_lo":0.14020433971028126,"chart":{"base":[382.3,63.1],"fp":[242.4,255.4],"lead":"62,263.5 272,241.9 482,219 692,171.5","note":{"base":"skill 0.26 — higher than 40% of cities","fp":"low end +4pp, high end +26pp","lead":"day-1 error 1.0 °C — better than 70% of cities","rel":"promised 0% → rained 2%; promised 97% → rained 69%"},"rel":"62.2,456.2 117.5,401 383.1,316.6 672,167.2"},"country":"AU","deep":false,"depth":["Rain-probability calibration","Calibration curve","Seasonal split"],"ece":0.10956325301204822,"ess":413.1933758556767,"html":{"answer":"\n<h2 id=\"answer\">The short answer for Canberra</h2>\n<div class=\"verdict\">\n<p class=\"lead\"><b>The Canberra rain forecast is moderately skilful, though 5 points on its probability scale are off by more than chance explains.</b></p>\n<p>When it says rain is <i>near certain</i> (97%), believe about\n<b>69%</b>. When it says rain is <i>very unlikely</i>\n(0%), there is still roughly a <b>2%</b> chance.</p>\n<p class=\"muted\">Based on 664 days, 2024-04-26 to\n2026-02-27. \"Rain\" means at least 0.2 mm measured at\nCANBERRA (AUSTRALIAN NATIONAL, 1.8 km from the forecast grid point.\nSkill score 0.26, ranked 128 of\n213 &mdash; but see the rank <i>range</i>\n(73&ndash;164) before reading anything into\nthat position.</p>\n</div>\n\n<h3>What the percentages actually mean here</h3>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th class=\"num\">It said</th><th class=\"num\">It rained</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Days</th><th>Verdict</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class='num'>0%</td><td class='num'><b>2%</b></td><td class='num'>265</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>4%</td><td class='num'><b>12%</b></td><td class='num'>67</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>14%</td><td class='num'><b>18%</b></td><td class='num'>66</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>35%</td><td class='num'><b>20%</b></td><td class='num'>65</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>66%</td><td class='num'><b>49%</b></td><td class='num'>68</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>97%</td><td class='num'><b>69%</b></td><td class='num'>133</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">5 of 6 groups are further from honest than chance\nalone can explain. The rest are indistinguishable from a perfect forecast.</p>\n","card":"\n<div class=\"gcard\">\n  <p class=\"gcard-head\"><b>Canberra</b> <span class=\"muted\">Australia</span></p>\n  <p class=\"gcard-tier\"><span class=\"tag ok\">Moderately skilful</span>\n    <span class=\"muted\">5 points off by more than chance</span></p>\n  <dl class=\"gcard-stats\">\n    <div><dt>Skill score</dt><dd>0.26</dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Rank</dt><dd>73&ndash;164\n      <span class=\"muted\">of 213</span></dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Record</dt><dd>664 <span class=\"muted\">days</span></dd></div>\n  </dl>\n  <p class=\"gcard-more\"><a href=\"#answer\">The full verdict for\n    Canberra &darr;</a></p>\n</div>","curve":"\n<h2 id=\"curve\">The calibration curve</h2>\n<p>Each dot is a group of days sharing a similar forecast. Horizontal position\nis what was promised; vertical is what happened. <b>On the dashed diagonal =\nhonest.</b> Hover any dot for its sample size.</p>\n<figure><svg viewBox=\"0 0 430 430\" width=\"100%\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Calibration curve for Canberra\"><rect class=\"chart-plot\" x=\"58\" y=\"18\" width=\"354\" height=\"364\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"58\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"382\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"58\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">0%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"386\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">0%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"146.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"146.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"291.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"291.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"146.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">25%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"295.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">25%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"235.0\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"235.0\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"200.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"200.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">50%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"204.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">50%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"323.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"323.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"109.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"109.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"323.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">75%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"113.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">75%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"412\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"18\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"412\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">100%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"22\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">100%</text><polygon class=\"chart-band\" points=\"58.1068679245283,380.6264150943396 70.41641791044776,349.4029850746269 108.25727272727273,299.27272727272725 183.42492307692308,214.0 290.9632352941177,103.64705882352945 400.74120300751883,20.73684210526318 400.74120300751883,39.89473684210526 290.9632352941177,183.94117647058826 183.42492307692308,292.4 108.25727272727273,359.93939393939394 70.41641791044776,382.0 58.1068679245283,382.0\" opacity=\"0.16\"/><line class=\"chart-ideal\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\" stroke-dasharray=\"5,4\" stroke-width=\"1.3\"/><line class=\"chart-base\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"292.09638554216866\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"292.09638554216866\" stroke-dasharray=\"2,3\"/><polyline class=\"chart-line\" points=\"58.1068679245283,373.7584905660377 70.41641791044776,338.53731343283584 108.25727272727273,315.8181818181818 183.42492307692308,309.2 290.9632352941177,205.35294117647058 400.74120300751883,130.21052631578948\" fill=\"none\" stroke-width=\"2.4\"/><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 0%&amp;#10;It rained 2% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 265 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"58.1068679245283\" cy=\"373.7584905660377\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 4%&amp;#10;It rained 12% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 67 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"70.41641791044776\" cy=\"338.53731343283584\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 14%&amp;#10;It rained 18% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 66 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"108.25727272727273\" cy=\"315.8181818181818\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 35%&amp;#10;It rained 20% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 65 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"183.42492307692308\" cy=\"309.2\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 66%&amp;#10;It rained 49% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 68 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"290.9632352941177\" cy=\"205.35294117647058\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 97%&amp;#10;It rained 69% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 133 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"400.74120300751883\" cy=\"130.21052631578948\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"422\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\">What the forecast promised</text><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"15\" y=\"200.0\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\" transform=\"rotate(-90 15 200.0)\">How often it actually rained</text></svg>\n<figcaption>Green band = where a <b>flawless</b> forecast would still land, given\nhow few days we have. Red dots fall outside it, so those are real errors rather\nthan noise. The faint horizontal line is climatology\n(25%).</figcaption></figure>\n","season":"\n<h2 id=\"season\">Does the season matter?</h2>\n<p>In Canberra the forecast is most skilful in\n<b>summer</b> (0.31) and least in\n<b>winter</b> (0.15).</p>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th>Season</th><th class=\"num\">Days</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Rain days</th><th class=\"num\">Skill score</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Avg error</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>winter</td><td class='num'>173</td><td class='num'>23%</td><td class='num'>0.149</td><td class='num'>11.5%</td></tr><tr><td>autumn</td><td class='num'>180</td><td class='num'>22%</td><td class='num'>0.278</td><td class='num'>9.2%</td></tr><tr><td>spring</td><td class='num'>127</td><td class='num'>21%</td><td class='num'>0.281</td><td class='num'>6.6%</td></tr><tr><td>summer</td><td class='num'>184</td><td class='num'>31%</td><td class='num'>0.309</td><td class='num'>11.2%</td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">Four-way splits of a two-year record are thin, so read the\nordering as indicative. Coarser binning is used here than for the annual curve\nfor the same reason.</p>\n"},"lat":-35.28346,"lon":149.12807,"n":664,"n_cities":213,"name":"Canberra","offset_days":-1,"pop_map":[{"hi":0.02,"lo":0.0,"mean":0.0003018867924528302,"n":265,"obs":0.022641509433962263,"sig":true},{"hi":0.065,"lo":0.02,"mean":0.03507462686567164,"n":67,"obs":0.1194029